.TH CBCBAYESPOSTPROC "1" "January 2026" "LALInference" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cbcBayesPostProc \- Generate a web page displaying results of parameter estimation based on the contents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cbcBayesPostProc.py
[\fI\,options\/\fR] \fI\,datafile.dat \/\fR[\fI\,datafile2.dat \/\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate a web page displaying results of parameter estimation based on the contents
of one or more datafiles containing samples from one of the bayesian algorithms (MCMC, nested sampling).
Options specify which extra statistics to compute and allow specification of additional information.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show this help message and exit
.TP
\fB\-o\fR DIR, \fB\-\-outpath\fR=\fI\,DIR\/\fR
make page and plots in DIR
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-data\fR
datafile
.TP
\fB\-i\fR INJ.XML, \fB\-\-inj\fR=\fI\,INJ\/\fR.XML
SimInsipral injection file
.TP
\fB\-t\fR COINC.XML, \fB\-\-trig\fR=\fI\,COINC\/\fR.XML
Coinc XML file
.TP
\fB\-\-skyres\fR=\fI\,SKYRES\/\fR
Sky resolution to use to calculate sky box size
.TP
\fB\-\-eventnum\fR=\fI\,NUM\/\fR
event number in SimInspiral file of this signal
.TP
\fB\-\-trignum\fR=\fI\,NUM\/\fR
trigger number in CoincTable
.TP
\fB\-\-bsn\fR=\fI\,BSN\/\fR
Optional file containing the bayes factor signal
against noise
.TP
\fB\-\-bci\fR=\fI\,BCI\/\fR
Optional file containing the bayes factor coherent
signal model against incoherent signal model.
.TP
\fB\-\-snr\fR=\fI\,SNR\/\fR
Optional file containing the SNRs of the signal in
each IFO
.TP
\fB\-\-dievidence\fR
Calculate the direct integration evidence for the
posterior samples
.TP
\fB\-\-boxing\fR=\fI\,BOXING\/\fR
Boxing parameter for the direct integration evidence
calculation
.TP
\fB\-\-evidenceFactor\fR=\fI\,FACTOR\/\fR
Overall factor (normalization) to apply to evidence
.TP
\fB\-\-ellipticEvidence\fR
Estimate the evidence by fitting ellipse to highestposterior points.
.TP
\fB\-\-plot\-2d\fR
Make individual 2\-D plots.
.TP
\fB\-\-header\fR=\fI\,HEADER\/\fR
Optional file containing the header line for posterior
samples
.TP
\fB\-\-ns\fR
(inspnest) Parse input as if it was output from
parallel nested sampling runs.
.TP
\fB\-\-Nlive\fR=\fI\,NLIVE\/\fR
(inspnest) Number of live points used in each parallel
nested sampling run.
.TP
\fB\-\-xflag\fR
(inspnest) Convert x to iota.
.TP
\fB\-\-ss\fR
(SPINspiral) Parse input as if it was output from
SPINspiral.
.TP
\fB\-\-spin\fR
(SPINspiral) Specify spin run (15 parameters).
.TP
\fB\-\-lalinfmcmc\fR
(LALInferenceMCMC) Parse input from LALInferenceMCMC.
.TP
\fB\-\-inj\-spin\-frame\fR=\fI\,INJ_SPIN_FRAME\/\fR
The reference frame used for the injection (default:
OrbitalL)
.TP
\fB\-\-downsample\fR=\fI\,DOWNSAMPLE\/\fR
(LALInferenceMCMC) approximate number of samples to
record in the posterior
.TP
\fB\-\-deltaLogL\fR=\fI\,DELTALOGL\/\fR
(LALInferenceMCMC) Difference in logL to use for
convergence test. (DEPRECATED)
.TP
\fB\-\-deltaLogP\fR=\fI\,DELTALOGP\/\fR
(LALInferenceMCMC) Difference in logpost to use for
burnin criteria.
.TP
\fB\-\-fixedBurnin\fR
(LALInferenceMCMC) Fixed number of iteration for
burnin.
.TP
\fB\-\-oldMassConvention\fR
(LALInferenceMCMC) if activated, m2 > m1; otherwise m1
> m2 in PTMCMC.output.*.00
.TP
\fB\-\-fm\fR
(followupMCMC) Parse input as if it was output from
followupMCMC.
.HP
\fB\-\-no\-acf\fR
.HP
\fB\-\-twodkdeplots\fR
.HP
\fB\-\-RconvergenceTests\fR
.HP
\fB\-\-nopdfs\fR
.TP
\fB\-c\fR COVARIANCEMATRICES, \fB\-\-covarianceMatrix\fR=\fI\,COVARIANCEMATRICES\/\fR
CSV file containing covariance (must give accompanying
mean vector CSV. Can add more than one matrix.
.TP
\fB\-m\fR MEANVECTORS, \fB\-\-meanVectors\fR=\fI\,MEANVECTORS\/\fR
Comma separated list of locations of the multivariate
gaussian described by the correlation matrix.  First
line must be list of params in the order used for the
covariance matrix.  Provide one list per covariance
matrix.
.TP
\fB\-\-email\fR=\fI\,user\/\fR@ligo.org
Send an e\-mail to the given address with a link to the
finished page.
.TP
\fB\-\-archive\fR=\fI\,results\/\fR.tar.gz
Create the given tarball with all results
.TP
\fB\-\-psdfiles\fR=\fI\,H1\/\fR,L1,V1
comma separater list of ASCII files with PSDs, one per
IFO
.TP
\fB\-\-kdecredibleregions\fR
If given, will use 2\-step KDE trees to estimate 1\-d
credible regions [default false: use greedy binning]
.TP
\fB\-\-noplot\-source\-frame\fR
Don't make 1D plots of source\-frame masses
